    <string name="settings_title_open_cores_selection">Choose emulators</string>
    <string name="settings_description_open_cores_selection">Pick which emulator (the program that plays the game) runs each system.</string>
    <string name="settings_core_selection_info">The first emulator for each system is the default and plays almost every game. The others are optional:\n\n• NES – Mesen: the most faithful to the real NES.\n• SNES – bsnes: more faithful than Snes9x, but needs a stronger device.\n• Game Boy / Color – SameBoy: as good as Gambatte, with nicer colours.\n• Game Boy Advance – gpSP: much lighter than mGBA, for games that run slowly.\n• Genesis / Mega Drive – PicoDrive: faster than Genesis Plus GX.\n• PlayStation – SwanStation: more faithful than PCSX ReARMed. It needs a PlayStation BIOS (a file from the real console) in Lemuroid/bios.\n• Nintendo DS – DeSmuME: only for old DeSmuME saves. melonDS is the default.\n\nPaprium always uses its own special emulator, whatever you pick for Genesis.\n\nSave slots only work with the emulator that made them. Saves made inside the game itself always carry over.</string>

