    <string name="mobile_settings_help">Help</string>
    <string name="lemuroid_help_content"><![CDATA[
        <b>Games not showing up?</b><br/>
        Allow "All files access". Unzip console games and put each system in its own folder, named like: $SYSTEMS. Then tap Scan for games.<br/>
        &#8226; PlayStation games also work in a PS, PS1 or PlayStation folder.<br/>
        &#8226; Arcade games stay zipped, in an Arcade, MAME, FBNeo or Neo Geo folder.<br/><br/>
        <b>The Lemuroid folder</b><br/>
        Lemuroid makes this folder on your phone. Inside: saves (your progress), states (save slots), bios (extra files some systems need, copied from the real console) and artwork (your own pictures for game tiles, named exactly like the game file; turn on Settings &#8594; Show artwork).<br/><br/>
        <b>Games with more than one disc</b><br/>
        Make a small text file ending in .m3u that lists the disc files, one per line, and put it next to them. The game then shows once. Change discs with Menu &#8594; Change disc.<br/><br/>
        <b>Handy tricks</b><br/>
        &#8226; Can\'t see the buttons on top of the game? Tap the top part of the screen.<br/>
        &#8226; Sound off? Press a volume key and the sound button appears.<br/>
        &#8226; Press and hold a game, then Start over, to play from the beginning instead of where you left off.<br/>
        &#8226; Scanlines look most even with Pixel-perfect scaling.<br/><br/>
        <b>Backups</b><br/>
        Settings &#8594; Backup puts everything in one zip file. It can also bring in saves from other emulators (.sav / .srm).
    ]]></string>

    <string name="lemuroid_crash_disclamer">The emulator ran into a problem and stopped. If it keeps happening, try this:\n• Press and hold the game and pick Start over, so it starts fresh instead of from the auto-save\n• Try another emulator in Settings → Choose emulators\n• Clear the app\'s cache in Android settings\n\nIf nothing helps, this game may not work with this emulator on your device.</string>


